{"id":"mahabharata-1-221","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":221,"title":"एकविंशत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 221 · Jarita and her fledglings face the fire","summary":{"en":"As the fire approaches, Jarita laments that she cannot carry her young to safety. She urges them to hide in a rat's hole, but the fledglings refuse, preferring death by fire to being eaten by the rat, and urge her to save herself.","kn":"ಅಗ್ನಿ ಸಮೀಪಿಸಿದಾಗ ಮರಿಗಳನ್ನು ಸುರಕ್ಷಿತ ಸ್ಥಳಕ್ಕೆ ಒಯ್ಯಲಾರೆನೆಂದು ಜರಿತೆ ವಿಲಪಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಇಲಿಯ ಬಿಲದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಡಗಿರಿ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಆದರೆ ಇಲಿಗೆ ಆಹಾರವಾಗುವುದಕ್ಕಿಂತ ಅಗ್ನಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸಾಯುವುದೇ ಲೇಸೆಂದು ಮರಿಗಳು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿ, ನೀನು ಉಳಿದುಕೋ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"आग निकट आने पर जरिता विलाप करती है कि वह बच्चों को सुरक्षित नहीं ले जा सकती। वह उन्हें चूहे के बिल में छिपने को कहती है, पर बच्चे चूहे का भोजन बनने के बजाय अग्नि में मरना पसन्द कर मना कर देते हैं और उसे स्वयं को बचाने को कहते हैं।","te":"అగ్ని సమీపించగా పిల్లలను సురక్షిత ప్రదేశానికి తీసుకువెళ్లలేనని జరిత విలపిస్తుంది. ఎలుక బొరియలో దాగమని చెబుతుంది, కానీ ఎలుకకు ఆహారం కావడం కంటే అగ్నిలో మరణించడమే మేలని పిల్లలు నిరాకరించి, నువ్వు తప్పించుకో అంటాయి.","ta":"தீ நெருங்கும்போது குஞ்சுகளைப் பாதுகாப்பாகக் கொண்டு செல்ல முடியவில்லையே என்று ஜரிதை புலம்புகிறாள். எலி வளையில் ஒளிந்துகொள்ளச் சொல்ல, எலிக்கு இரையாவதைவிடத் தீயில் இறப்பதே மேல் என்று குஞ்சுகள் மறுத்து, நீ தப்பித்துக்கொள் என்கின்றன.","ml":"തീ അടുക്കുമ്പോൾ തന്റെ കുഞ്ഞുങ്ങളെ രക്ഷപ്പെടുത്താൻ കഴിയാത്തതിൽ ജരിത വിലപിക്കുന്നു. ഒരു എലിമാളത്തിൽ ഒളിക്കാൻ അവൾ അവരോട് പറയുന്നു, എന്നാൽ എലി തിന്നുന്നതിനേക്കാൾ തീയിൽ മരിക്കുന്നതാണ് നല്ലതെന്ന് ഇളം പക്ഷികൾ വിസമ്മതിക്കുകയും, അമ്മ സ്വയം രക്ഷപ്പെടാൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.221; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"खाण्डवदाहपर्व","titleEn":"Khandavadaha Parva (Burning of the Khandava forest)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः प्रज्वलिते शुक्रे शार्ङ्गकास्ते सुदुःखिताः ।\nव्यथिताः परमोद्विग्ना नाधिजग्मुः परायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the bright fire blazed up, those Sharngaka fledglings, in great distress and trembling, found no refuge."}},{"n":2,"text":"निशाम्य पुत्रकान्बालान्माता तेषां तपस्विनी ।\nजरिता दुःखसंतप्ता विललाप नरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her small sons, their mother, the ascetic Jarita, burning with grief, wailed, O lord of men."}},{"n":3,"text":"अयमग्निर्दहन्कक्षमित आयाति भीषणः ।\nजगत्संदीपयन्भीमो मम दुःखविवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This terrible fire, burning the undergrowth, comes from there, setting the world ablaze, fearsome and increasing my grief."}},{"n":4,"text":"इमे च मां कर्षयन्ति शिशवो मन्दचेतसः ।\nअबर्हाश्चरणैर्हीनाः पूर्वेषां नः परायणम् ।\nत्रासयंश्चायमायाति लेलिहानो महीरुहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And these little ones, dull of mind, wingless and footless, who are the refuge of our forefathers, drag at me. This fire comes frightening the trees as it licks them."}},{"n":5,"text":"अशक्तिमत्त्वाच्च सुता न शक्ताः सरणे मम ।\nआदाय च न शक्तास्मि पुत्रान्सरितुमन्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My sons, lacking strength, cannot move with me, and I cannot take them and go somewhere else."}},{"n":6,"text":"न च त्यक्तुमहं शक्ता हृदयं दूयतीव मे ।\nकं नु जह्यामहं पुत्रं कमादाय व्रजाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor can I abandon them; my heart is aching. Which son should I leave, and which should I take and go?"}},{"n":7,"text":"किं नु मे स्यात्कृतं कृत्वा मन्यध्वं पुत्रकाः कथम् ।\nचिन्तयाना विमोक्षं वो नाधिगच्छामि किंचन ।\nछादयित्वा च वो गात्रैः करिष्ये मरणं सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"What should I do, my children, how do you think it should be done? Thinking of your escape I find no way at all. I will cover you with my body and die with you."}},{"n":8,"text":"जरितारौ कुलं हीदं ज्येष्ठत्वेन प्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nसारिसृक्वः प्रजायेत पितॄणां कुलवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father said to me, Jaritari will be the eldest and uphold the family; Sarisrikva will have children and increase the line of the ancestors;"}},{"n":9,"text":"स्तम्बमित्रस्तपः कुर्याद्द्रोणो ब्रह्मविदुत्तमः ।\nइत्येवमुक्त्वा प्रययौ पिता वो निर्घृणः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stambamitra will practice austerity; Drona will be the best knower of Brahman. Having said so, your father went away pitiless."}},{"n":10,"text":"कमुपादाय शक्येत गन्तुं कस्यापदुत्तमा ।\nकिं नु कृत्वा कृतं कार्यं भवेदिति च विह्वला ॥","meaning":{"en":"With whom shall I be able to go, whose misfortune is the greatest? What should I do so that the task is done? she said, bewildered."}},{"n":11,"text":"नापश्यत्स्वधिया मोक्षं स्वसुतानां तदानलात् ।\nएवं ब्रुवन्तीं शार्ङ्गास्ते प्रत्यूचुरथ मातरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With all her wits she could not see how to save her sons from the fire. As she spoke so, the Sharngaka fledglings answered their mother."}},{"n":12,"text":"स्नेहमुत्सृज्य मातस्त्वं पत यत्र न हव्यवाट् ।\nअस्मासु हि विनष्टेषु भवितारः सुतास्तव ।\nत्वयि मातर्विनष्टायां न नः स्यात्कुलसंततिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give up your love, mother, and fly to where the fire does not reach. If we are lost, you will have other sons; if you, mother, are lost, we shall have no line of our family."}},{"n":13,"text":"अन्ववेक्ष्यैतदुभयं क्षमं स्याद्यत्कुलस्य नः ।\nतद्वै कर्तुं परः कालो मातरेष भवेत्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Considering both, whichever is best for our family, mother, this is the right moment for you to do it."}},{"n":14,"text":"मा वै कुलविनाशाय स्नेहं कार्षीः सुतेषु नः ।\nन हीदं कर्म मोघं स्याल्लोककामस्य नः पितुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not let your love for your sons destroy our family; this act of our father, who wished for the worlds, must not be in vain."}},{"text":"जरितोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Jarita said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"इदमाखोर्बिलं भूमौ वृक्षस्यास्य समीपतः ।\nतदाविशध्वं त्वरिता वह्नेरत्र न वो भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Near this tree there is a mouse's hole in the ground. Enter it quickly; there you have no fear of the fire."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततोऽहं पांसुना छिद्रमपिधास्यामि पुत्रकाः ।\nएवं प्रतिकृतं मन्ये ज्वलतः कृष्णवर्त्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I will cover the hole with dust, my sons; I think that is a defense against the blazing fire."}},{"n":17,"text":"तत एष्याम्यतीतेऽग्नौ विहर्तुं पांसुसंचयम् ।\nरोचतामेष वोपायो विमोक्षाय हुताशनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After the fire has passed I will come and scatter the heap of dust. Let this plan please you, as a way to escape the fire."}},{"text":"शार्ङ्गका ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The Sharngakas said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अबर्हान्मांसभूतान्नः क्रव्यादाखुर्विनाशयेत् ।\nपश्यमाना भयमिदं न शक्ष्यामो निषेवितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A flesh-eating mouse would destroy us, wingless and made of mere flesh. Seeing this danger, we cannot go in there."}},{"n":19,"text":"कथमग्निर्न नो दह्यात्कथमाखुर्न भक्षयेत् ।\nकथं न स्यात्पिता मोघः कथं माता ध्रियेत नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could the fire not burn us, how could the mouse not eat us? How could our father's act not be in vain, and how could our mother be kept safe?"}},{"n":20,"text":"बिल आखोर्विनाशः स्यादग्नेराकाशचारिणाम् ।\nअन्ववेक्ष्यैतदुभयं श्रेयान्दाहो न भक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the hole we face destruction by the mouse, in the air by the fire; considering both, being burned is better than being eaten."}},{"n":21,"text":"गर्हितं मरणं नः स्यादाखुना खादता बिले ।\nशिष्टादिष्टः परित्यागः शरीरस्य हुताशनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Death by a mouse eating us in a hole would be shameful, while giving up the body to fire is prescribed by the good."}}]}]}